    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q116">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1843"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q83"/>
        <cpr:P4 rdf:resource="https://www.ctc-n.org/technologies/breakwaters"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1160">
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1164"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1165"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1166"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q894"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q672"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q62"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q65"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Working people who are disproportionately impacted by climate change or the response to climate change. This can be because the risks of their profession are elevated by climate change; because their social status in general makes them more vulnerable to climate change; or because their profession is likely to change or even disappear due to the green transition.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1161">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q986"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1164">
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1520"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1160"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1012"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1571"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q764"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q856"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">People whose occupation makes them more likely to be adversely impacted by climate change. Sometimes, these are jobs which are inherently risky -- for example, fire risk for firefighters or health risks for healthcare workers -- and the magnitude and/or frequency of those risks are increasing due to the effects of climate change. A large share of the increased risk however is due to heat stress from increasing temperatures, as well as air pollution and vector borne diseases.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1165">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1160"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q760"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q802"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q804"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q809"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q810"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q814"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q905"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q908"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q909"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q911"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q912"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">People whose job is at risk due to the societal changes necessary to respond to climate change. Often, this is because they work in an industry that either is heavily reliant on fossil fuels, such as the plastics industry, or that creates products which are reliant on fossil fuels, such as cars.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1166">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1160"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1167"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">People who usually do physical work and usually do not have much money nor a very high level of formal education. This means that, on average, they have more limited means to respond to the effects of climate change and therefore are likely to be impacted more severely by it.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1167">
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1012"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1166"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1168"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1169"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q683"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q701"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q894"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q672"/>
        <cpr:P20 xml:lang="en">h5v7ggyq</cpr:P20>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q913"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q994"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q997"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">People who are less able to respond to the effects of climate change due to having limited financial or physical assets. In practice, this encompasses a wide variety of people whose vulnerabilities may overlap.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1168">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1167"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">people living in cities or suburban areas with limited assets, including financial assets. This includes people who are experiencing hardship due to structural underinvestment in their neighbourhood and those who struggle due to a lack of services and a relatively high cost of living.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1169">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1167"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Adults and young adults who have received no or little education from schools or universities. Generally, this makes them more susceptible to climate impacts.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q117">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1843"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q83"/>
        <cpr:P4 rdf:resource="https://www.ctc-n.org/technologies/jetties"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1170">
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1016"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1602"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q676"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q701"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q704"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q672"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1248"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q913"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">people and groups of people with no or limited power, or who are frequently excluded by other parts of society</cpr:P7>
        <cpr:P9 xml:lang="en">non-discrimination</cpr:P9>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1172">
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q690"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q695"/>
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q708"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q672"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">people whose physiology or health makes them more likely to be impacted by climate change. Note that this includes mental health, even though this is not strictly physical</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1173">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q988"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1174">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q987"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1175">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q519"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1176">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q519"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1177">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q519"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q836"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1178">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q519"/>
        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1574"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1179">
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1180"/>
