    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q146">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1846"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1860"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2550"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Fungal symbiosis is a symbiotic relationship between a fungus and a photosynthetic bacteria or algae. The cells from the alga or bacterium live inside the fungus. Besides providing a home, the fungus also provides nutrients. In turn, the bacterium or the alga provides energy to the fungus by performing photosynthesis. Fungal symbiosis can enhance ecosystem resilience and reduce the negative impact of increased precipitation on nutrient losses.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
