    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q147">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1613"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1860"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2550"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Crop diversification refers to the practice of growing a variety of different crops on the same agricultural land, rather than focusing on a single crop. This strategy is used to reduce the risks associated with farming, such as those caused by pests, diseases, or unpredictable weather patterns. It also helps improve soil health, increase biodiversity, and provide a more stable income for farmers.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
