    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1624">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q131"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1623"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Approach that sustainably increases agricultural productivity and incomes, adapts and builds resilience to climate change, and reduces greenhouse gas emissions where possible. CSA systematically considers the synergies and tradeoffs that exist between productivity, adaptation, and mitigation. It encompasses a range of practices and technologies that are tailored to specific agro-ecological conditions and socio-economic contexts including the adoption of climate-resilient crop varieties, conservation agriculture techniques, agroforestry, precision farming, water management strategies, and improved livestock management.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
