    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2541">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1851"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2546">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q140"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2555">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1625"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Synthetic fertilisers contribute to greenhouse gas emissions during both their production and application. They are manufactured through energy-intensive processes that rely heavily on fossil fuels. When nitrogen fertilisers are applied to soil, some of the nitrogen is absorbed by plants, while some is processed by soil microorganisms, which release nitrous oxide (N₂O) as a by-product of their metabolic processes. Synthetic nitrogen fertilisers are estimated to account for approximately 2.1% of global emissions.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2556">
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2682"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2508"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2565">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q362"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">A rotational grazing system comprises a series of pastures that are used at various times, on a rotational basis, based on weather and forage availability. Consequently, each of the pastures is at a different stage of growth compared to its counterparts. Periods of rest and regrowth are critical in allowing pasture species time to build energy stores and root reserves.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2566">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q362"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">A stocking rate is the amount of grazing animals allocated to a certain area of land. It is typically expressed in animals per hectare (livestock units per hectare) and applies mainly to cattle. A correct stocking rate will achieve high, long-term farm profitability.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2578">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q144"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Hydroponic cultures use water-based nutrient solutions or granulate substrates, which include peat moss, charcoal, gravel, rock wool, perlite, coco peat, and coconut coir. Main advantages of hydroponics are optimization of resources, recycling and reutilization of nutrient solutions, high yields, and reduction of the risk of soil-borne pests and diseases.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2579">
        <cpr:P1 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1858"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1952"/>
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2593"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Reducing food loss and waste with efficient management practices at the distribution, retail and consumption levels. Measure mainly involve efficient technologies for quality preservation, optimization of transport and supply chains, and awareness-raising.</cpr:P7>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2581">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1994"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q2583">
        <cpr:P2 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q1994"/>
    </rdf:Description>
